Chapter: CceBands

 The CCE character predicates, for the transpiler plugs. This chapter
 deliberately CITES NOTHING: a chapter that cites Foreword chapter CCE
 resolves the chapter definition and would be transpiled as ordinary
 user code, which tests nothing about the emitters. Citing nothing is
 what routes these three calls to each plug's own builtin emission.

 CCE numbers its code points by frequency, so every probe below is a
 code that separates a CCE band from the ASCII or Unicode one an
 emitter might reach for instead. 15 is the letter a and 12 is a digit;
 in Unicode 15 is a control character and 12 is a form feed, so an
 emitter that hands the code point to a Unicode predicate answers F
 where this file wants T. 70 is punctuation and sits in the hole
 between the two letter bands, and 97 is an accented Latin letter in
 the upper band.

  cb-letter : Integer -> Text
  cb-letter (n) = if is-letter (code-to-char n) then "T" else "F"

  cb-digit : Integer -> Text
  cb-digit (n) = if is-digit (code-to-char n) then "T" else "F"

  cb-ws : Integer -> Text
  cb-ws (n) = if is-whitespace (code-to-char n) then "T" else "F"

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni ("letter 12,15,70,97=" & cb-letter 12 & cb-letter 15 & cb-letter 70 & cb-letter 97)
   print-line-uni ("digit 2,3,12,13=" & cb-digit 2 & cb-digit 3 & cb-digit 12 & cb-digit 13)
   print-line-uni ("ws 0,1,2,3=" & cb-ws 0 & cb-ws 1 & cb-ws 2 & cb-ws 3)
  end

